   "sentence": 1,
   "start": 0.0,
   "word_start": 0.0,
   "speech_end": 7.38,
   "text": "In the nineteen eighties, an inventor from Ohio named Stanley Meyer built a small dune buggy, and claimed it ran on nothing but water.",
   "first_word": "In",
   "asr_first": "In",
   "end": 7.94,
   "onset": 0.25
  },
  {
   "sentence": 2,
   "start": 7.94,
   "word_start": 7.92,
   "speech_end": 12.56,
   "text": "He said his 'water fuel cell' split water into hydrogen and oxygen, and burned them as fuel.",
   "first_word": "He",
   "asr_first": "He",
   "end": 13.02,
   "sil": [
    7.47,
    8.0
   ],
   "onset": 8.0
  },
  {
   "sentence": 3,
   "start": 13.02,
   "word_start": 13.0,
   "speech_end": 17.74,
   "text": "He claimed the car could drive from Los Angeles to New York on just twenty-two gallons of water.",
   "first_word": "He",
   "asr_first": "He",
   "end": 18.2,
   "sil": [
    12.69,
    13.08
   ],
   "onset": 13.08
  },
  {
   "sentence": 4,
   "start": 18.2,
   "word_start": 18.24,
   "speech_end": 20.48,
   "text": "Investors believed him, and handed him their money.",
   "first_word": "Investors",
   "asr_first": "Investors",
   "end": 21.04,
   "sil": [
    17.85,
    18.26
   ],
   "onset": 18.26
  },
  {
   "sentence": 5,
   "start": 21.04,
   "word_start": 21.02,
   "speech_end": 28.08,
   "text": "In nineteen ninety-six, expert witnesses examined his fuel cell for an Ohio court, and found nothing revolutionary at all.",
   "first_word": "In",
   "asr_first": "In",
   "end": 28.08,
   "sil": [
    20.58,
    21.1
   ],
   "onset": 21.1
  },
  {
   "sentence": 6,
   "start": 28.08,
   "word_start": 28.08,
   "speech_end": 33.02,
   "text": "The court ruled it was 'gross and egregious fraud', and ordered him to pay the investors back.",
   "first_word": "The",
   "asr_first": "The",
   "end": 33.42,
   "sil": [
    28.32,
    28.42
   ],
   "onset": 28.42
  },
  {
   "sentence": 7,
   "start": 33.42,
   "word_start": 33.44,
   "speech_end": 38.26,
   "text": "Physics agrees: splitting water takes more energy than you ever get back by burning the hydrogen.",
   "first_word": "Physics",
   "asr_first": "Physics",
   "end": 38.95,
   "sil": [
    33.22,
    33.57
   ],
   "onset": 33.57
  },
  {
   "sentence": 8,
   "start": 38.95,
   "word_start": 38.96,
   "speech_end": 44.82,
   "text": "In nineteen ninety-eight, Meyer collapsed at a restaurant, and witnesses said he cried, 'They poisoned me.'",
   "first_word": "In",
   "asr_first": "In",
   "end": 45.41,
   "sil": [
    38.49,
    39.01
   ],
   "onset": 39.01
  },
  {
   "sentence": 9,
   "start": 45.41,
   "word_start": 45.4,
   "speech_end": 48.78,
   "text": "But the coroner found he died of a brain aneurysm, from natural causes.",
   "first_word": "But",
   "asr_first": "But",
   "end": 49.26,
   "sil": [
    44.96,
    45.47
   ],
   "onset": 45.47
  },
  {
   "sentence": 10,
   "start": 49.26,
   "word_start": 48.78,
   "speech_end": 53.12,
   "text": "Still, to this day, some people believe his water car was hidden from the world.",
   "first_word": "Still",
   "asr_first": "Still,",
   "end": 53.92,
   "sil": [
    49.01,
